<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  AI-assisted: Claude Opus 5.5 (xhigh effort) via Claude Code, 2026-10-10: wrote the URDF/xacro, launch file and tests;
  moved these properties out of the hand-written car_props.xacro (values and comments unchanged) when gen_props.py
  took car_props.xacro over; after a third review, corrected the stated source of the stand-in masses (the comments
  had credited all four to "project defaults, M2.T4"; camera and IMU are the Module 6 guide's). No value changed.
  AI-assisted: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code, 2026-10-16: took the plate outline from a classmate's CAD of the Emo chassis
  plate (wing depth 40 -> 34.35 mm, plate ends fitted to the CAD length, CAD thickness, and the rounded front's two
  radii); every other value is unchanged.
  AI-assisted: Claude Opus 5.5 (xhigh effort) via Cursor, 2026-10-29: took the mass-distribution inputs from the M1.T16
  weighing (caster_load 0.142 -> 0.058 kg, drive_wheels_load 0.364 -> 0.602 kg, the com_x comment for the middle-value
  decision), added the power-bank box (bank_*), moved the photo ESTIMATE motor_x_min from -0.016 to -0.015 m so the
  gearbox boxes end at the measured bank front face, and updated the sources and the stale comments; after a review
  the same day, added bank_top_h (rounded), stated the com_x range from the readings alone (8.8 to 11.2 mm) and who
  decided what, reworded the motor_x_min clipping as an agent decision, and labelled the private-repo files. No value
  changed in that review. The readings are Xiaohui Chen's.

  car_geometry_extras.xacro: the car geometry that configs/car.json (M1.T9, schema bm.car/1) does NOT carry, one
  xacro:property per value. HAND-WRITTEN, not generated. gen_props.py writes car_props.xacro from car.json;
  beaconmind_car.urdf.xacro includes car_props.xacro and then this file. No property may be defined in both files
  (test_props_files_do_not_overlap), because a later xacro definition would silently replace the earlier one.

  Sources: course-project/evidence/M1/M1.T9/measurements-2026-10-29-with-m1t16-mass.csv holds every row used here
  (test_urdf.py reads it as this file's source CSV). It is built up in three dated layers:
    - 2026-10-10: readings by Xiaohui Chen, an unchanged copy of assignments/assignment6/measurements.csv, a file of the
      private course repo that is not in this public repo (the copy is
      course-project/evidence/M1/M1.T9/measurements-xiaohui-chen-2026-10-10.csv). The photos (assignments/assignment6/photos/)
      and the dispositions (assignments/assignment6/review/MEASUREMENT-REVIEW.md) cited below are in the private repo too.
    - 2026-10-16: the PLATE OUTLINE rows (plate_front_x, plate_rear_x, plate_strip_width, wing_depth, plate_thickness, the
      two front radii), from a classmate's CAD of the plate and B1/B2 fitted to its length (the private course repo
      (plate CAD is not published here)), labelled CAD or fit below; first in measurements-2026-10-16-with-plate-cad.csv.
    - 2026-10-29: the M1.T16 rows (readings by Xiaohui Chen, course-project/evidence/M1/M1.T16/measurements.md): the
      weighing K1_total_mass_remeasure / K2_caster_load_remeasure / K2_drive_wheels_load_remeasure and the power-bank
      box B15_bank_*.
  Where the CSV has a later row for the same quantity (suffix _corrected, _recheck, _remeasure, _remeasure2) the later
  row is used; rows marked SUPERSEDED are not inputs; C3_caster_swivel_axis_x replaces the earlier photo estimate of
  the swivel x.
  If a row used here is re-measured, edit this file by hand. Values that car.json carries are changed in car.json
  (course-project/tools/write_car_json.py) and regenerated with gen_props.py, never here.

  Conventions (M2.T4 / README C1), the same as car_props.xacro:
    base_link = midpoint between the two drive-wheel centres, AT AXLE HEIGHT (z = 0 at the axle).
    +x = toward the camera lens / caster end (the car's front). +y = robot left. +z = up.
    model z = floor height - wheel_radius. Lengths in metres, masses in kg, angles in radians.
    Values named *_h are heights above the FLOOR; the URDF converts them with "- wheel_radius".

  Labels used below:
    measured  = a row of measurements.csv (row name given), with its uncertainty.
    CAD       = a dimension of the classmate's plate CAD (row of the 2026-10-16 CSV, instrument "CAD"), +-0.5 mm allowance.
    fit       = a 2026-10-10 reading adjusted to agree with a CAD dimension (row of the 2026-10-16 CSV, instrument "fit").
    derived   = arithmetic on measured rows (shown).
    ESTIMATE  = read off a photo or a vendor-typical size; provisional, re-measure before trusting.
    ASSUMED   = not measured at all; a placeholder.
    stand-in  = a mass not weighed: wheels and caster as M2.T4 step 5 gives them; camera and IMU the Module 6 guide's
                values (derived-values.md "guide defaults"; M2.T4 gives none). Details at the masses below.
  Uncertainty: single ruler readings +-2 mm, "around" readings +-5 mm (review #11).
-->
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">

  <!-- ================= Plate (clear acrylic) ================= -->
  <!-- The overall extents axle_to_front, axle_to_rear and body_width, and the main-body height chassis_height, come
       from car.json through car_props.xacro. -->
  <!-- 2026-10-16: the plate outline now follows a classmate's CAD of the same Emo chassis plate (Onshape STEP and
       drawing DRW_MOBILE_ROBOT_CHASSIS, the private course repo (plate CAD is not published here)), whose hole pattern matches this car's
       plate on the bottom-view photo to 0.25 mm rms (photo-check.txt there). The rows are in
       course-project/evidence/M1/M1.T9/measurements-2026-10-16-with-plate-cad.csv and, unchanged, in
       measurements-2026-10-29-with-m1t16-mass.csv (the CSV car.json names since 2026-10-29).
       CAD = a dimension of the model, +-0.5 mm allowance; fit = the 2026-10-10 ruler readings B1/B2 fitted to the
       CAD plate length 206.98 mm. -->
  <!-- fit B1_plate_front_x_corrected = 130.49 mm: axle line to the plate's front apex (131 mm ruler reading, less half
       of the 1.02 mm by which B1 + B2 exceeded the CAD length); +-3 mm (axle datum, review #15) -->
  <xacro:property name="plate_front_x" value="0.13049"/>
  <!-- fit B2_plate_rear_x_corrected = 76.49 mm (77 mm reading, same fit), written as a signed x coordinate; +-3 mm -->
  <xacro:property name="plate_rear_x" value="-0.07649"/>
  <!-- CAD B5_plate_width_narrow_corrected = 100 mm, the strip from the wing to the front (the ruler read 100 too);
       +-0.5 mm -->
  <xacro:property name="plate_strip_width" value="0.100"/>
  <!-- CAD B5b_wing_depth_centre_corrected = 34.35 mm, rear apex to the wing shoulder (x -76.49 to -42.14); +-0.5 mm.
       Replaces the 40 mm ruler reading (review #7 had flagged it; the photo, mapped onto the CAD, gives 34.0 mm). -->
  <xacro:property name="wing_depth" value="0.03435"/>
  <!-- The wing's rear edge is a half-ellipse with semi-axes wing_depth (x) by body_width / 2 (y): the CAD's ELLIPSE
       74.04 x 34.35 mm, cut where it meets the shoulder fillets at |y| = 73.95 mm, so body_width / 2 = 73.96 mm (the
       2026-10-10 photo fit IMG_7436/7440 had found the same shape). beaconmind_car.urdf.xacro draws it as
       wing_slices stepped slices and COMPUTES each slice width from wing_depth and body_width (ellipse width at the
       slice's mid-depth), so a re-measured wing needs no hand-typed widths. With 34.35 x 73.96 mm and 4 slices:
       71.6 / 115.5 / 137.1 / 146.8 mm. -->
  <xacro:property name="wing_slices" value="4"/>
  <!-- CAD P1_plate_front_arc_radius = 135.14 mm and P2_plate_front_corner_radius = 8 mm: the plate's front edge is one
       arc whose apex is plate_front_x, joined to each side of the strip by an 8 mm fillet; +-0.5 mm each.
       beaconmind_car.urdf.xacro ends the full-width strip where the fillets start (x = 115.35 mm) and draws the
       rounded front as front_slices stepped slices, each as wide as the outline at the slice's middle
       (3 slices: 99.2 / 89.2 / 52.0 mm). -->
  <xacro:property name="plate_front_arc_radius" value="0.13514"/>
  <xacro:property name="plate_front_corner_radius" value="0.008"/>
  <xacro:property name="front_slices" value="3"/>
  <!-- measured B8_plate_underside_h_front = 46 mm (caster end) and B8_plate_underside_h_rear = 43 mm (wing end),
       floor; +-2 mm each. -->
  <xacro:property name="plate_underside_h_front" value="0.046"/>
  <xacro:property name="plate_underside_h_rear" value="0.043"/>
  <!-- derived: the plate is modelled LEVEL (the 0.8 +- 0.4 deg nose-up tilt is not significant, review #12) at the
       MEAN of the two B8 readings, (46 + 43) / 2 = 44.5 mm floor; +-1.5 mm. The level plate is then within 1.5 mm
       of both measured heights. -->
  <xacro:property name="plate_underside_h" value="${round((plate_underside_h_front + plate_underside_h_rear) / 2, 6)}"/>
  <!-- CAD: plate thickness 3.000 mm (STEP solid, z 0 to 3 mm; drawing "3"); +-0.5 mm. Until 2026-10-16 this was an
       ESTIMATE from photos IMG_7437 / IMG_7438 (3 mm +-1 mm). -->
  <xacro:property name="plate_thickness" value="0.003"/>
  <!-- measured B9_lowest_body_h = 30 mm: bottom of the TT motor gearboxes (floor); re-measured, upheld by review #2; +-2 mm.
       car.json chassis_height_m (= chassis_height) is B10_battery_holder_top_h 66 - B9 30 = 36 mm; beaconmind_car.urdf.xacro
       stops if chassis_height and battery_top_h - lowest_body_h disagree.
       Since 2026-10-29 the power bank (bank_bottom_h = 17 mm, below) is the car's lowest body point, not the gearboxes.
       This property stays the GEARBOX bottom: it is the bottom of the motor boxes and one term of the chassis_height
       guard, and chassis_height_m is deliberately unchanged (M1.T16 decision, evidence/M1/M1.T16/measurements.md). -->
  <xacro:property name="lowest_body_h" value="0.030"/>

  <!-- ================= Parts on and under the plate ================= -->
  <!-- TT motor gearboxes (one per side), under the plate, long axis along x.
       z: measured B9 (bottom 30 mm floor) to the plate underside (44.5 mm floor, derived above).
       x: ESTIMATE (photo IMG_7436 bottom view, scaled from the shaft at the tyre centre) - provisional: gearbox rear
          end about 16 mm behind the axle, encoder end about 58 mm ahead; +-6 mm.
          2026-10-29: the rear end is drawn at 15 mm behind the axle (-0.015), within the +-6 mm of the photo estimate
          (-16 mm): it is clipped to the power bank's MEASURED front face (B15_bank_front_x, x = -15 mm) so that the
          gearbox boxes (|y| 29 to 51 mm) and the bank box do not share volume. Whether the two parts touch on the car
          is not measured. This 1 mm change is an agent decision (Claude Opus 5.5, 2026-10-29) for Xiaohui to accept.
          At -0.016 the boxes would share 1 x 6 x 12 mm, and the bank/motor guard in beaconmind_car.urdf.xacro stops
          xacro. Still an ESTIMATE.
       y: ESTIMATE (IMG_7436 shows |y| about 27-52 mm; vendor-typical TT gearbox width 22 mm) - provisional:
          |y| 29 to 51 mm, which stays 2.5 mm clear of the tyre inner face at |y| = 53.5 mm; +-4 mm. -->
  <xacro:property name="motor_x_min" value="-0.015"/>
  <xacro:property name="motor_x_max" value="0.058"/>
  <xacro:property name="motor_y_inner" value="0.029"/>
  <xacro:property name="motor_y_outer" value="0.051"/>

  <!-- USB power bank (a black block, 70 x 70 x 25 mm, lying flat) under the plate at the breadboard end (the back),
       fixed with 3M double-sided tape to the plate underside. Readings by Xiaohui Chen, 2026-10-29 (M1.T16,
       course-project/evidence/M1/M1.T16/measurements.md; rows B15_bank_*).
       GEOMETRY ONLY (M1.T16 decision): no link and no mass of its own. The bank was not weighed alone, so its mass stays
       inside the measured total (car.json mass_kg, hence chassis_mass) and chassis_link's uniform-box inertia.
       x: measured B15_bank_front_x = 15 mm and B15_bank_rear_x = 85 mm BEHIND the axle line, written as signed x;
          +-3 mm each (axle-datum floor, review #15). 85 - 15 = 70 mm, the bank's side. The rear face is 8.5 mm behind
          the plate's rear apex (plate_rear_x = -76.49 mm), but car.json rear_overhang_m, corners and sweep_radius_m are
          deliberately NOT updated yet: the rear Pico cable reaches 148 mm behind the axle and the front camera cable is
          unmeasured, and Xiaohui decides the footprint later. The bank's rear corners are 91.9 mm from the axle
          midpoint, inside the 0.140 m sweep radius.
       width: measured B15_bank_width = 70 mm (the 70 x 70 mm footprint); +-2 mm.
       y: measured: centred (Xiaohui), 18 mm from the bank to each tyre (B15_bank_tyre_gap; (107 - 70) / 2 = 18.5 mm);
          +-2 mm.
       bottom: measured B15_bank_bottom_h = 17 mm floor; +-2 mm. The car's lowest body point (the gearboxes are at 30 mm).
       height: measured B15_bank_height = 25 mm (vertical size); +-2 mm. Top 17 + 25 = 42 mm floor, under the plate
          (43 mm measured at this end, B8_plate_underside_h_rear; 44.5 mm in the level model): the tape fills the gap. -->
  <xacro:property name="bank_x_min" value="-0.085"/>
  <xacro:property name="bank_x_max" value="-0.015"/>
  <xacro:property name="bank_width" value="0.070"/>
  <xacro:property name="bank_bottom_h" value="0.017"/>
  <xacro:property name="bank_height" value="0.025"/>
  <!-- derived: bank top above the floor = bank_bottom_h + bank_height = 42 mm, rounded to 1 um as body_box rounds, so
       the guards that compare it with a touching face do not misfire on float noise (0.005 + 0.025 gives
       0.030000000000000002). Used by the guards and by the power_bank box. -->
  <xacro:property name="bank_top_h" value="${round(bank_bottom_h + bank_height, 6)}"/>

  <!-- Breadboard: two 400-point boards snapped side by side, one rail strip removed
       (reference/hardware/car-build-notes.md), on the plate over the rear wing; rows 1-30 run along x (row 1 at the
       rear, row 30 over the motors).
       top: measured B10_breadboard_top_h = 55 mm floor; +-2 mm. Bottom = plate top (44.5 + 3 mm).
       x: measured B12_breadboard_rear_x = -70 mm and B12_breadboard_front_x = +20 mm; +-2 mm each.
       width: measured B12_breadboard_width = 100 mm; +-2 mm.
       y: ESTIMATE - provisional: centred on y = 0 (not measured; IMG_7436 suggests 2-4 mm to the robot's right). -->
  <xacro:property name="breadboard_x_min" value="-0.070"/>
  <xacro:property name="breadboard_x_max" value="0.020"/>
  <xacro:property name="breadboard_width" value="0.100"/>
  <xacro:property name="breadboard_top_h" value="0.055"/>

  <!-- 4 x AA battery holder, flat, cells along x, on the plate at the front, between the breadboard and the ESP32-CAM.
       top: measured B10_battery_holder_top_h = 66 mm floor; +-2 mm. Bottom = plate top.
       x: measured B13_battery_holder_rear_x = +40 mm and B13_battery_holder_front_x = +100 mm; +-2 mm each.
       width: measured B13_battery_holder_width = 63 mm; +-2 mm.
       y: ESTIMATE - provisional: centred on y = 0 (not measured; IMG_7436 shows it about central). -->
  <xacro:property name="battery_x_min" value="0.040"/>
  <xacro:property name="battery_x_max" value="0.100"/>
  <xacro:property name="battery_width" value="0.063"/>
  <xacro:property name="battery_top_h" value="0.066"/>

  <!-- ESP32-CAM on its ESP32-CAM-MB base, flat on the plate at the front, USB-C forward, in front of the battery holder.
       x: derived - from the battery holder's front (B13 +100 mm; IMG_7437 shows the two touching) to the measured
          front-most point B3_front_most_x = +138 mm (= axle_to_front, no cable): 38 mm long, so the two boxes
          share a face and do not overlap. +-3 mm.
       width: measured B14_esp32cam_width = 20 mm; +-2 mm. FLAG: narrower than the vendor-typical ESP32-CAM board
          (27 mm, not a source recorded in this repo); re-check if the camera's clearance ever matters.
       y: ESTIMATE - provisional: centred on y = 0 (the lens above it is measured on the centre line, S3_lens_y = 0).
       top: measured B14_esp32cam_front_top_h = 61 mm floor (highest point at the board's front edge), used as the
          top of the whole stack; +-2 mm. -->
  <xacro:property name="esp32_x_min" value="${battery_x_max}"/>
  <xacro:property name="esp32_width" value="0.020"/>
  <xacro:property name="esp32_top_h" value="0.061"/>

  <!-- Grey LEGO Technic camera stand, standing on the ESP32-CAM board behind the camera module.
       top: measured B10_camera_stand_top_h = 100 mm floor ("around 10 cm"); +-5 mm.
       section 8 x 8 mm: ESTIMATE (one Technic beam is 8 mm wide) - provisional.
       x: ESTIMATE - provisional: directly behind the 6 mm camera module, i.e. from camera_x - 14 mm to camera_x - 6 mm. -->
  <xacro:property name="stand_top_h" value="0.100"/>
  <xacro:property name="stand_section" value="0.008"/>
  <xacro:property name="camera_module_depth" value="0.006"/>
  <!-- ESTIMATE (vendor-typical OV3660 / OV2640 camera module, about 8.5 mm square) - provisional; visual only -->
  <xacro:property name="camera_module_size" value="0.0085"/>

  <!-- BNO055 board (Adafruit 2472): 20 x 27 mm (reference/hardware/bno055-pin-map.md section 5).
       Orientation (derived from the sources, not measured on the car): in reference/hardware/bno055-top.jpg both
       header rows (6 holes Vin..RST, 4 holes PS0..ADR) run along the board's LONG 27 mm edges, about 0.7 inch apart
       across the 20 mm width. car-build-notes.md seats the 6-pin row in ONE breadboard column (g) over rows 1-6,
       and breadboard rows run along x (row 1 at the rear). So the 27 mm side is along x and the 20 mm side along y,
       with the two rows straddling the board's centre gap. With the measured centre x = -61 mm the board spans
       x -74.5 to -47.5 mm, overhanging the breadboard's rear edge (-70) by about 4.5 mm, as a board held on its pins
       can. Bottom of the box = breadboard top (the header spacer fills the gap); top = imu_top_h. -->
  <xacro:property name="imu_board_size_x" value="0.027"/>
  <xacro:property name="imu_board_size_y" value="0.020"/>

  <!-- ================= IMU orientation ================= -->
  <!-- The IMU position (imu_x, imu_y, imu_top_h, imu_z) comes from car.json through car_props.xacro.
       ASSUMED, not measured (board taken as flat and square to the car; car.json has no imu_axes yet); M1 IMU
       calibration will set them. -->
  <xacro:property name="imu_roll" value="0.0"/>
  <xacro:property name="imu_pitch" value="0.0"/>
  <xacro:property name="imu_yaw" value="0.0"/>

  <!-- ================= Caster swivel ================= -->
  <!-- measured C3_caster_swivel_axis_x = 120 mm: axle line to the centre of the caster's round swivel plate (the
       pivot), the re-measure review #3 / #4 asked for; +-2 mm. Replaces the earlier photo estimate (115 mm).
       Used for the centre-of-mass lever arm (below) and for the fork visual in the URDF.
       OPEN, not used in the model: the swung-forward readings C2b_caster_front_swung_x = 127 mm (disputed, review #4)
       and its re-measures C2b_..._remeasure = 135 mm and C2b_..._remeasure2 = 140 mm imply a swivel offset of only
       (140 - 12.5) - 120 = 7.5 mm, against 20 mm from C3 and the trailing contact C2 = 100 ("around", probably the
       looser reading). The caster sphere stays at the measured trailing contact C2 = 100 mm (car.json caster_x_m);
       the footprint sweep (ROBOT_RADIUS) uses 140 mm, the worst measured front. -->
  <xacro:property name="caster_swivel_x" value="0.120"/>

  <!-- ================= Mass distribution ================= -->
  <!-- The total, mass = K1_total_mass_remeasure = 660 g (2026-10-29, M1.T16; 506 g until then), comes from car.json
       mass_kg through car_props.xacro. The lever rule below needs the caster load and the total from ONE weighing:
       both are the M1.T16 weighing. The one-weighing guard in beaconmind_car.urdf.xacro stops xacro when
       caster_load + drive_wheels_load and car.json's mass differ by more than 2.5 g, and test_com_matches_lever_rule
       checks the same sum on the CSV rows. -->
  <!-- measured K2_caster_load_remeasure = 58 g (2026-10-29, M1.T16: caster on one scale, NOT turned sideways, which way
       it trailed unknown); +-1 g. Was K2_caster_load = 142 g on 2026-10-10 (caster turned sideways, review #3). -->
  <xacro:property name="caster_load" value="0.058"/>
  <!-- measured K2_drive_wheels_load_remeasure = 602 g (2026-10-29, both drive wheels on the other scale; 58 + 602 = 660 g,
       the single-scale K1 reading); +-1 g. Was K2_drive_wheels_load = 364 g on 2026-10-10. -->
  <xacro:property name="drive_wheels_load" value="0.602"/>
  <!-- derived (lever rule). Xiaohui's decision of 2026-10-29 (evidence/M1/M1.T16/measurements.md "Decisions for M2.T4"):
       use the middle value, x = 0.0105 m ahead of the axle, +-0.0018 m. The model implements it (agent wording) with the
       caster's swivel x as the lever arm: whole-car centre of mass x = C3_caster_swivel_axis_x x K2_caster_load_remeasure
       / K1_total_mass_remeasure = 120 x 58 / 660 = 10.545 mm.
       Why a range: the caster was NOT turned sideways on its scale this time, so its load acted at its floor contact,
       not at the swivel pivot, and which way it trailed is unknown.
         - The +-1.8 mm ASSUMES the 20 mm trail of the 2026-10-10 notes (pivot C3 120 mm, trailing contact C2 about
           100 mm): trailing toward the axle 100 x 58 / 660 = 8.788 mm, trailing forward 140 x 58 / 660 = 12.303 mm,
           so the swivel x is the middle, +-1.758 mm.
         - From the readings alone the forward contact is at most about 127.5 mm: C2b_caster_front_swung_x_remeasure2
           puts the wheel FRONT at about 140 mm with the caster swung fully forward, and the caster radius is 12.5 mm
           (the 2026-10-10 trail conflict, review #4, is still open). That gives 8.8 to 11.2 mm
           (127.5 x 58 / 660 = 11.205 mm).
         The chosen 10.545 mm lies inside both intervals, so the value does not change.
       Smaller terms: each mm of C3 (+-2 mm) moves it 58 / 660 = 0.088 mm, and each g on the caster scale about 0.18 mm.
       Re-weighing with the caster turned sideways (the 2026-10-10 method) removes the range. (2026-10-10, caster turned
       sideways: 120 x 142 / 506 = 33.676 mm.)
       Kept to 9 decimals so that the URDF reproduces it within 1e-6 m (test_com_matches_lever_rule). -->
  <xacro:property name="com_x" value="${round(caster_swivel_x * caster_load / mass, 9)}"/>
  <!-- ESTIMATE - provisional, not measured: chassis centre-of-mass height = middle of the main body
       (30 to 66 mm floor = 48 mm floor), i.e. 48 - 33.5 = 14.5 mm above the axle; +-10 mm.
       Still an unmeasured estimate after 2026-10-29: the power bank (17 to 42 mm floor, centre 29.5 mm floor, below)
       may pull the true height down, within the +-10 mm; no reading fixes it (the bank was not weighed alone). -->
  <xacro:property name="chassis_com_z" value="0.0145"/>
  <!-- stand-in masses, NOT weighed; the chassis gets the remainder (beaconmind_car.urdf.xacro chassis_mass), now
       0.660 - 2 x 0.030 - 0.010 - 0.010 - 0.005 = 0.575 kg (0.421 kg with the 2026-10-10 total of 0.506 kg).
       wheel_mass 30 g each and caster_mass 10 g: M2.T4 step 5 ("mass 0.03 kg each (stand-in)", caster "mass 0.01 kg").
       camera_mass 10 g and imu_mass 5 g: the Module 6 guide defaults (assignments/assignment6/derived-values.md line 41,
       a private course repo file; the instructor's model, guide-original/urdf/gazebo_car.urdf.xacro, also in the
       private course repo, gives camera_link 0.01 and imu_link 0.005 kg).
       M2.T4 step 5 gives the camera and IMU links no mass, and its chassis mass is mass - 2 x 0.03 - 0.01 = 0.590 kg
       (0.436 kg in 2026-10-10 terms); this model's 0.575 kg also subtracts these two (a recorded deviation,
       evidence/M2/M2.T4/README.md). The stand-in values are unchanged by the M1.T16 update. -->
  <xacro:property name="wheel_mass" value="0.030"/>
  <xacro:property name="caster_mass" value="0.010"/>
  <xacro:property name="camera_mass" value="0.010"/>
  <xacro:property name="imu_mass" value="0.005"/>

</robot>
